{
  "_comment": [
    "Classification table for OCI referrer descriptors, built from OBSERVED DHI",
    "attestations rather than from spec assumptions. Source of truth for this table:",
    "scripts/90-inspect-referrers.sh run against nicksdemoorg/dhi-node across six",
    "tags (alpine, debian, fips, sfw-ent variants) on 2026-08-07.",
    "",
    "WHAT WAS ACTUALLY FOUND, and why it shapes this file:",
    "",
    "1. Every DHI attestation carries artifactType application/vnd.in-toto+json.",
    "   NOTHING is distinguishable by artifactType. The document type appears only",
    "   in the in-toto.io/predicate-type annotation, so predicateTypes below do all",
    "   the real work and artifactTypes are near-useless for DHI.",
    "",
    "2. Attestations attach to PER-PLATFORM manifest digests, not to the index.",
    "   Querying referrers on the index digest returns ZERO. 20-verify.sh queries",
    "   both the index and platform digests and merges.",
    "",
    "3. OpenVEX is NOT universal. Observed on debian-based tags (26-debian13,",
    "   22-debian13-fips) and ABSENT on alpine-based tags (24-alpine,",
    "   24-alpine-fips, 24-alpine-sfw-ent-dev). VEX therefore sits in",
    "   expectedGroups, not requiredGroups: requiring it would fail every Alpine",
    "   DHI image. Set REQUIRE_VEX=1 to promote it to a hard requirement.",
    "",
    "4. Neither vulnerability attestation contains VEX assessments.",
    "   in-toto/vulns/v0.2 holds only {scanner, metadata}; scout/vulnerabilities",
    "   holds a plain findings list with CVSS but no status/justification fields.",
    "   They are NOT a substitute for VEX and are deliberately not mapped to the",
    "   vex group -- deriving VEX from a findings list would invent claims the",
    "   vendor never made.",
    "",
    "predicateTypes match by PREFIX, so https://slsa.dev/provenance covers both",
    "/v0.2 and /v1 without listing each version."
  ],

  "requiredGroups": ["sbom", "provenance"],
  "expectedGroups": ["vex"],

  "classes": [
    {
      "id": "sbom-spdx",
      "label": "SPDX SBOM",
      "requiredGroup": "sbom",
